From: "A.Cervantez" <155030226+Ywach404@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:49:49 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] bridge: let the metal backend finish at exit

The game never releases its D3D9 device when it quits, so the metal
backend's release path, which writes its pipeline archive and logs the
pipeline summary, never ran: a real session opened a new archive and
left nothing on disk. rt_gfx_report runs at every traced exit, so in
metal mode it now resolves metal_d3d9_shutdown from the backend and
calls it before its own report. A backend without the export is left
alone, so older builds of it still load.
---
 shims/d3d9_bridge.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/shims/d3d9_bridge.c b/shims/d3d9_bridge.c
index f6c2c05..34f3335 100644
--- a/shims/d3d9_bridge.c
+++ b/shims/d3d9_bridge.c
@@ -2640,6 +2640,15 @@ static int cmp64(const void *x, const void *y)
 
 void rt_gfx_report(void)
 {
+    /* The game quits without releasing its device, and the metal
+       backend writes its pipeline archive and summary at release, so
+       neither would happen. It does both here instead, before this
+       report, so its lines land with the rest of the exit. Resolved
+       late and optional: a backend without the export just skips it. */
+    if (s_mode == RT_GFX_METAL && s_lib) {
+        void (*shutdown)(void) = (void (*)(void))dlsym(s_lib, "metal_d3d9_shutdown");
+        if (shutdown) shutdown();
+    }
     uint32_t n = s_nframes;
     double q[4] = {0, 0, 0, 0};
     uint64_t *v = n ? malloc(n * sizeof *v) : NULL;
